ce again  another concept or idea introduced in  early dragon ball that will become  exceptionally popular later in z  and z used to tremendous effect right  here in this scene to achieve one thing  to place goku in a position of mystery  and control throughout this tournament  no matter what match was taking place in  the quarterfinals goku would remark upon  each encounter with tremendous insight  and observation skills lending to the  idea that he is more in control and more  powerful than even we as an audience  might appreciate and that very aspect of  the story being told through this fight  is emphasized through this very action  he's been concealing his power from both  his opponent and us the readers or  viewers ten shinhan remarks beforehand  that he's impressed by goku's  improvement but that his speed is still  nothing compared to his own leading him  to outmaneuvering goku at every turn  however despite this two things remained  consistent goku never got tired and goku  never had a problem tracking his  movements and this all starts to make  sense when you realize he wasn't able to  move as fast as he wanted to placing  goku once again on another level above  everyone else which isn't an unfamiliar  position for him to be in during these  tournaments throughout the 21st and 22nd  tenkaichi budokai a key aspect of these  tournaments surrounding goku has been  that of how competent he actually is and  the stories surrounding them have been  discussing how best to overcome the  mountain he presents to the likes of  roshi and others however what makes this  arc unique when taking that aspect into  account is that unlike the previous arcs  where goku is the obstacle in this arc  goku is the point of view character the  hero we see his internal thoughts as he  tries to piece together what's going on  between shen and piccolo and even tens  shinhan and tao and that's what makes  this ark so special he's not the  obstacle piccolo is and right now  tenchinon is blocking the way to piccolo  and that long sought after a first place  spot strongest under the heavens  needless to say things aren't looking  too good for the crane school alumni but  what i really like about this section is  that tin shinhan doesn't roll over and  take this sudden show ability by goku as  an indication that he's lost he'll know  he's the defending champion instead in  response to that he whips out a move no  one has ever seen before including goku  in the past we've seen after image  techniques and we've even seen  tenshinhan grow extra limbs in the prior  bout three years ago but this time he  takes that to its natural conclusion by  splitting himself into four separate but  identical fighters and the presence of  this scene serves two purposes one to  demonstrate how tenacious gifted and  hardworking tenchinon is as a fighter  and two to show us all that goku not  only has developed physically as made  obvious earlier in the fight but that he  has sharpened his mind greatly also  i really appreciated the angle this  fight has taken it places goku once  again in the driver's seat and creates  all of this anticipation with his very  statement alone begging us the readers  to try and figure out what those two  weaknesses might actually be that he's  talking about overall this fight  delivers on just about every front it's  a terrific settling of a score produce  some wonderful paneling and showcase  some clever action writing with the  weaknesses goku exposes in this  technique not only making sense but  because they made sense it only further  cemented how much more adept a fighter  goku has become over the last three  years goku advances to the finals in  dominating fashion next up  shen versus piccolo jr  with one match between two rivals now  having reached its conclusion we press  onward to another between kami  inhabiting the body of a civilian named  shen versus the reincarnation of the  demon king his other half piccolo jr and  while it's one of the shortest  semi-final matchups its design is simple  but immensely effective these  semi-finals while interesting in their  own right with some interesting action  set pieces were designed with the clear  mission of establishing and building up  the contestants of the final match up  above all else with this fight against  shen used to outstanding effect in  helping to elevate piccolo higher than  we ever could possibly have foreseen  something you might have noticed during  this review however is that despite  having acknowledged piccolo as the main  villain of the ark i've not done much in  the way of speaking about him beyond his  relationship to kami and that's with  good reason if you were to go back  through the previous arc and this one to  compare the two incarnations of their  respective piccolos the king and the  reincarnation you'd notice that while  sharing some ideological similarities  they are markedly different piccolo jr  throughout these contests seems to have  shown some respect to his fellow  competitors on some level during  numerous fights either while watching or  participating piccolo acknowledges the  power and toughness of his opponents  going as far as to admit what he's been  proven wrong this isn't something king  piccolo would ever have done with him at  the first sign of resistance pushing  back or losing his mind to blinding  anger however when piccolo is taken  aback and shown resistance he applies  strategy and counter measures  [Music]  the fight itself is littered with some  interesting back and forth with some  telling pieces of dialogue and actions  taken it's an effective fight lending  opportunity to develop piccolo raise the  stakes of the event and even at times  elevates goku in subtle ways during the  shen vs piccolo fight on the first page  of chapter 181 after seeing the  breakneck pace of the opening to this  match everyone is left stunned roshi  krillin tenshinhan yamcha everyone  except for goku without words this helps  him stand out from the crowd ahead of  his match in the finals and on the topic  of the finals match there's a brief but  interesting back and forth between kami  and goku right before he goes out to  fight piccolo in the semi-finals and  within it the pieces are set for goku to  become the character he will remain for  quite some time into z and beyond  throughout this series goku has been a  character that when faced with  expectation and reality shatters those  expectations innovating new ways around  problems people never thought possible  at present kami doesn't think goku has  what it takes to do what he thinks he  needs to to kill piccolo jr and goku  doesn't want to kill piccolo knowing it  will in turn kill kami and there my  friends lie is the main problem of this  arc piccolo has sealed kami inside a  vial and swallowed it and now goku is  the only fighter remaining to protect  the world from the wrath of this  sinister individual but if the last  number of arcs and indeed these last  couple of fights have taught us anything  about goku is that when he's backed up  against a corner and given two options  he's the sort of character to grit his  teeth dig deep and create a third to  find another way when no one else could  this is what i call a true heroes moment  and it's all coming to a head for the  finals of the 23rd tenkaichi budokai the  finals  piccolo junior vs son goku  of all the fights in dragon ball none  other better signal the rise of the  younger generation more so than this  right here goku who surpassed his older  master and piccolo who's just dominated  kami and it all comes to a head in the  finals of a best tournament in the  series it's established early on that  goku is fighting with a self-imposed  handicap well okay actually too not only  does he want to defeat piccolo but he  needs to protect the spectators  surrounding him and in addition to that  he still wants to win the tournament all  this time as an audience we've been  focused on piccolo and the threat he  presents overcoming him and freeing kami  but goku  he just might do it something of note  also during this match is that the  battle contains the inspiration for some  of the most iconic moments and set  pieces from goku's fight with vegeta  take for example their beam struggle  during the gorge battle it's iconic but  the exact same scene took place with the  exact same framing in this battle with  piccolo and if that wasn't enough  remember goku's battle with uzaru vegeta  one massive difference between these two  battles with giant opponents is how the  scene serves goku or depicts him for  lack of a better term in the vegeta  fight as many of you might remember goku  is firmly on the back foot which  admittedly has its own benefits in it  creating additional tension moving  towards the climax but in this piccolo  fight the size disparity isn't used to  overwhelm goku but to instead subvert  the audience and prop goku up and  demonstrate how tough he is and how  intelligent he can be he openly refuses  any help from anyone else like  tenshinhan or krillin citing it as  grounds for disqualification something  he's actively trying to avoid while  trying to defend himself against piccolo  but perhaps most impressively and what  makes me prefer this version of this set  piece more is how goku uses it to  manipulate his opponent to create new  solutions never before thought of when  goku is faced with a hopeless situation  he will create a solution no one thought  was possible and he did so here not just  with his strength but with his strategy  and intelligence this is how you  communicate to your reader or viewer  that your character is strong that he's  a powerful individual not with big  numbers or screaming but showing us  firsthand the effort and misdirection he  forces piccolo to work through it's an  impressive display placing goku on a  pedestal alongside piccolo at this  moment it truly feels as though two  demigods are duking it out with no other  living being even remotely coming close  demonstrating innovations on techniques  i didn't even know i wanted like firing  the kamehameha with his feet allowing  him to free up his hands for a punch  it's incredible the creativity on  display here and despite everything  that's on the line time and again he's  forced to deny the help of anyone that  interferes now while a great and  impressive part of the story concerns  itself with goku overcoming the odds and  managing to unleash more and more  ability and power his friends never  thought he had the other half of this  battle is supplied by piccolo who in  turn shows his own brand of toughness  and grit to push through whether that be  the strength he demonstrates the  techniques he amazes us with or the  secret abilities of his race it seems  this character can create his own  alternative options when all others are  taken off the table and this tough  tenacious dynamic piccolo brings to the  table for goku brings out the best in  his character both need this victory so  much is hanging in the balance and  despite all of this goku still refuses  to treat this like anything other than a  tournament and this moment this right  here this is where goku stole piccolo's  soul it's in this moment goku steam  rising off of him and clothes tattered  after taking the very best piccolo has  to throw at him remains standing upright  before him smiling what an outrageously  brilliant fight after taking the  absolute best this warrior has goku  rallies himself one last time and with  fear in piccolo's eyes the young man  sprints towards the would-be demon king  landing a devastating elbow to his jaw  it's honestly difficult not to just sit  back and commentate over all of this  fight the panels surrounding this  section of the manga are some of the  best in the series and even our son  toyotaro himself took inspiration for  his dragon ball super manga the poses  are just incredibly dynamic the layouts  are incredible  the entire story of early dragon ball  has centered around a specific  philosophy  to not train to win but to better  yourself and to protect those that are  defenseless in the 21st tenkaichi  budokai roshi desperately wanted to  instill this lesson in the young warrior  and in doing so learned that goku was  something truly special even when he was  a small boy he could see that there was  something outstanding waiting to be  tapped into even back then it was  apparent he wasn't like the others  pushing his master to his absolute  limits in the 22nd tenkaichi budokai and  beyond goku gained the responsibility  that such power brings with it not  because he wanted it but because it was  who he was and in the face of that  alongside a new generation roshi hung up  his ghee for good for the first time in  many many many years a young boy was  able to stand up when others couldn't  and save the world three years pass now  a young man goku's limp body lays  defeated on the ground before piccolo  who's now celebrating his conquest of  the earth and in no more fitting a  fashion as kami rallies the remaining  earth's defenders to intervene life  surges back into goku  this  is what makes goku special in the face  of certain death without any usable  limbs and every option taken from him he  still finds it in him to dig deep smile  and invent a solution to the impossible  problems that stand before him no matter  how formidable no matter how terrifying  no matter the stakes no matter the odds  goku will find a way to succeed when  others can't  [Applause]  the winner of the 23rd tenkaichi budokai  is son goku  this arc sandwiched between two time  skips contains more passion skill vision  and love in many other acts in this  series and indeed many other stories  i've ever read i started this video  series in the hopes that it would shed  some light on why i loved this story so  much and i hope i've managed to  introduce at least a few of you to what  i consider to be one of the most  underrated stories to have come out of  japan this was a much needed enjoyable  trip down memory lane for me i haven't  had the best year and a half but this  story definitely has lifted my spirits  in times when nothing else could i thank  you so much for taking the time out of  your days to share it with me i don't  know what the future holds but i'm  excited i hope i'll see you there i'd  also like to thank tfs for contributing  to this video in the best of ways they  are some of the nicest most  accommodating individuals to work with  and you can find everything from their  personal twitters to their youtube  channels down below in the description
 

